            <ArticleTitle>Metagenome of the Siberian Underground Water Reservoir.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e01317-17</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/genomeA.01317-17</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on the metagenome of a deep subsurface aquifer in the Tomsk region of Russia, sampled via an oil exploration borehole drilled to a depth of 2.8 km. Methanogenic archaea were present in the water along with members of various bacterial phyla, including Firmicutes, Chloroflexi, Bacteroidetes, Ignavibacteriae, and uncultured candidate divisions.</AbstractText>
